### Describe the bug

According to the [MDN: function](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/JavaScript/Reference/Statements/function#description)
> Like let, in strict mode, [function declarations are scoped to the most closely containing block](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/JavaScript/Reference/Statements/function#block-level_function_declaration).

However, It seems that swc handle function scope incorrectly.

### Input code

```typescript
const k = (() => {
  function x() { console.log("hi") }
  {
    function x() { console.log("merong") }
  }
  return x;
})();
k();
```


